; One channel of the frequency card, entered by hand.
FORM CHANNEL
TITLE Channel and frequency
SUMMARY Enters or changes one channel of your frequency card by hand, for a region with no documents. The frequency is kept like an imported one and never shown again; left blank on a channel already held, it is kept.
LEVEL ZERO
ORDER 40
ACTION channel_put
PREFILL channel name
FIELD name Designator(X) required upper max=12 check=designator
FIELD frequency Frequency(X) secret check=frequency
FIELD unit Unit(KHZ,MHZ,HZ) default=KHZ
FIELD mode Mode(USB,LSB,ALE,DATA,AM,FM,CW)
FIELD use What it is for(X) upper max=40
FIELD ant_rx RX antenna, tuner port(1,2)
FIELD ant_tx TX antenna, tuner port(1,2)
FIELD world World(MARS,AMATEUR)
FIELD label HFLink label(X) upper max=16
NEXT CHANNEL SCHEDULE
BEGIN_HELP
Designator:
The name everyone uses for the channel, as on the card: P1, S1. Only the designator is ever sent in the clear.
END

Frequency:
As on the card. It is kept on this box and goes out only sealed to a checked member's card. A new channel needs one; leave it blank to keep the one a channel already has.
END

Mode:
The sideband or mode the channel is worked in, as on the card. The radio is keyed in this mode. Blank keeps the mode the channel has (USB for a new one).
END

What it is for:
PRIMARY, SECONDARY, SCAN. No frequency here.
END

RX antenna, tuner port:
Tuner port this channel listens on, 1 or 2. Selected on a channel change, with RF off. Blank keeps the port the channel has (1 for a new one).
END

TX antenna, tuner port:
Tuner port this channel transmits on, 1 or 2. The tuner switches to it before each transmit and back to RX after, with RF off. Tunes and tuner memories are on this port. Blank keeps the port the channel has (1 for a new one).
END

World:
MARS or AMATEUR. The message center sends and routes only on MARS channels; an amateur channel is there to listen on. Blank keeps what the channel has (MARS for a new one).
END

HFLink label:
An amateur channel's everyday name, never a frequency. Blank keeps the label a channel has.
END
